From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 13:58:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] protocol: serialize the address binding report feature

VP_ANDROID_17_requirements lists VK_EXT_device_address_binding_report. It
defines no command, so listing it is the whole change and the extension table
grows from 203 entries to 204.

Only VkPhysicalDeviceAddressBindingReportFeaturesEXT gets codecs.
VkDeviceAddressBindingCallbackDataEXT does not, and cannot: it chains onto
VkDebugUtilsMessengerCallbackDataEXT, and the protocol carries no debug
messenger callback at all, because Venus answers VK_EXT_debug_utils out of the
guest driver rather than forwarding it. A report that a host driver raises has
no path to a guest messenger, so this entry makes the feature queryable and
the extension enableable; it does not make a host driver's reports visible to
a guest application.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 vn_protocol.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/vn_protocol.py b/vn_protocol.py
index f9cdf30e0f9b56cc0e5f29807ea0d8ca556d2fc5..4f8554b0eab9eee63500254b7eb0c336e5b8f722 100755
--- a/vn_protocol.py
+++ b/vn_protocol.py
@@ -168,6 +168,7 @@ VK_XML_EXTENSION_LIST = [
     'VK_EXT_depth_clip_enable',
     'VK_EXT_depth_range_unrestricted',
     'VK_EXT_descriptor_heap',
+    'VK_EXT_device_address_binding_report',
     'VK_EXT_dynamic_rendering_unused_attachments',
     'VK_EXT_extended_dynamic_state3',
     'VK_EXT_external_memory_acquire_unmodified',
